  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer planar dielectric coating on fused silica substrate with air incidence at normal angle (0 degrees). The coating stack alternates HfO2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) layers, starting with HfO2 at the air interface and ending with SiO2 (Lemarchand) at the substrate interface, for 24 total coating layers. Optimize all 24 individual layer thicknesses within bounds [20, 200] nm. Initialize thicknesses within ±10% variance around the best thickness vector from iteration-08 (candidate opt_24layer_dual_band_high_R_low_R__172eaad160ed). Apply 25% reduction to mutation step-size compared to prior rounds. Execute deterministic local refinement (Nelder-Mead) on top-5 candidates before resuming stochastic mutation. Use coherent transfer-matrix method. Evaluate performance across two wavelength bands: 300-450 nm (target: maximize reflectance) and 1000-1700 nm (target: maximize transmittance). Score candidates using dual-band equal-weight objective. Material optical constants (n, k) are read from the material catalog datasets for hfo2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand); they are not design variables. Total layer count is fixed at 24. Polarization is unpolarized at normal incidence.",
